cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to Pilovo, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "Pilovo"
abstract: >-
  Pilovo is an open-source Chrome extension (Manifest V3, MIT license) that
  shows whether the ChatGPT and Claude web tabs you authorize are working, have
  a response ready, need your attention or cannot be confirmed. It lists them
  in Chrome's side panel and counts the items to review on its toolbar badge,
  so you can return to the right tab. Pilovo observes a limited set of status indicators
  locally, with optional access per site, and does not collect your prompts,
  responses or tab titles. Version 0.4.0 is an experimental preview installed
  manually from GitHub; it is not on the Chrome Web Store. Pilovo is an
  independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by the companies that
  operate ChatGPT or Claude.
authors:
  - name: "Pilovo contributors"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: 2026-10-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/alebgl77/pilovo"
url: "https://github.com/alebgl77/pilovo"
keywords:
  - "Chrome extension"
  - "Manifest V3"
  - "side panel"
  - "ChatGPT"
  - "Claude"
  - "local-first"
  - "privacy"
